# Release lines (ENG-2110)

Read before touching `versions/`, `release/`, `scripts-release/`, a `release-*.yml` workflow,
`pr-checks.yml`, `sdk-build.yml`, `.github/sdk.env`, or anything that decides what version a
build reports. This is the contract the repo files encode. The human runbooks are
`docs/release-lines.md` and `docs/release-admin-setup.md`. The model is the ds-tegra-distro
release-line process (its `.ai/release-lines.md` and `docs/release-lines.md`); this repo runs the
same jobs ported to one product, one repository, and install-tree tarballs built against the
exported SDK instead of OS images.

## The rule this port exists for

Nothing in this repository's CI acts on another repository. The build reads (this checkout with
the job token, the pinned schemas commit with `REPO_ACCESS_TOKEN`, the SDK installer from S3;
never a push, tag, dispatch or PR elsewhere), and every `actions/create-github-app-token` step
has exactly `repositories: ${{ github.event.repository.name }}`. `pr-checks.yml` fails a PR that
names `meta-dsensos` or `ds-tegra-distro` in a `release-*.yml` or in `scripts-release/`, that
dispatches into another repo, that widens a token, or whose `sdk-build.yml` dispatches, mints an
App token or writes to a repository. A ds release reaches an OS image only through the OS
layer's own pin bump (`DSREV` and `DS_BRANCH` in `conf/distro/include/ds-src-pins.inc`, its
`bump-app-pin.yml` workflow or a person), then the lockfile bump in ds-tegra-distro. App lines
and OS lines are independent: an OS line pins whichever app line it chooses (`main`, `N.x.x`,
`N.M.x`), and this repo follows an OS line only for its SDK (`.github/sdk.env`, below). The OS
repos' lockstep lines, `base.yml` branch names, lockfile pins and the sync job have no
counterpart here and must not grow one.

## Lines, tags, versions

- `release/config.json`: `{"products": ["ds"], "product_prefix": false, "bookkeeping_files":
  [".github/sdk.env"], "artifact": {"kind": "install-trees", "services": [every recipe in
  `containers/sdk-build.sh` ORDER, kept equal to it by hand], "info_file": "sdk-build-info.txt"}, "version_probe":
  {"path": "./ds-cot-xlate/opt/ds/bin/cot-xlate", "pattern": "{version}"}}`. `artifact.kind` is
  `debs` or `install-trees` and the other keys depend on it (`debs`, `deb_arch`,
  `deb_version_rule` and a probe with `deb` under `debs`, which is sensor-portal's shape; the two
  key sets never mix, and the old top-level deb keys are refused). `version.py config` prints it
  with defaults, `version.py check` validates it together with `versions/` and
  `release/matrix.json` (`{"products": {"ds": {"flavors": ["ds_ds-arm64_release"]}}}`, flavors
  are `<product>_<machine>_<type>` and the machine token is the S3 prefix, not the SDK MACHINE).
- With `product_prefix: false` (this repo) the lines are `main` (major), `N.x.x` (minor, cut from
  tag `vN.0.0`), `N.M.x` (patch, cut from `vN.M.0`). `scripts-release/lines.py parse` classifies a
  name; anything with a `/` (`dev/main`, `release/vl`) or like `1foo.x.x` is kind `none` and the
  rc-build `plan` job skips it. Parent of `N.M.x` is `N.x.x` when that branch exists, else `main`;
  parent of `N.x.x` is `main`. The code keeps the prefixed mode of the reference working so the
  copies of the tooling stay one code base; nothing here uses it.
- Tags: release `vX.Y.Z` (a GitHub release on it), RC pre-release `rc/<sha7>`, one per green
  push. The old hand-made `v*` tags are history; immutable releases, once on, burn a deleted
  release's tag name, so creating jobs default `dry_run=true`.
- `versions/ds` is the pending version: the version the next promote on this branch tags, one
  `X.Y.Z` line, written only by the jobs with `[skip ci]` (create-branch's opening commit, the
  post-promote bump). Promote on `main` tags the pending version and bumps the major
  (`AUTO_LEVEL`, unchanged from the reference); on `N.x.x` the minor; on `N.M.x` the patch.
  `bump=major|minor|patch` overrides. After `v1.0.0` the pending on `main` is `2.0.0`; minor
  releases come from a `1.x.x` line.
- Version strings: dev `X.Y.Z-dev.<N>.g<sha7>[.dirty]` (every build not given a version), RC
  `X.Y.Z-rc.<N>.github-<sha7>` (`N = git rev-list --count`, so RCs of one version order), release
  `X.Y.Z`. Lowercase, never `+`. Deb `Version` fields (the portal, and the OS layer's packages of
  these services) take the dpkg form from `version.py deb-version`: the first `-` becomes `~`,
  later ones `.` (`1.1.0~rc.5.github.abc1234` sorts before `1.1.0`, as SemVer intends; a plain
  `-` would make the RC sort after the release).
- Into the binaries: `containers/cmake/ds-version.cmake`, `ds_version(DS)`, called by the
  containers root, utils, cot_translator and mqtt_translator. A non-empty `-DDS_BUILD_VERSION`
  (from `containers/sdk-build.sh --build-version`, which CI passes, or from the OS layer's
  `ds-versioning` class on an image build) wins, with `-DDS_RELEASE_LINE` beside it. Otherwise
  the tag rule: an exact `vX.Y.Z` tag on a clean HEAD gives `X.Y.Z`, anything else gives the dev
  string from `versions/ds` and git. `scripts-ci/build-version.sh` (the same script as
  sensor-portal's) is the shell form of the same rule, and the driver uses it for the dev
  string. The module sets `DS_VERSION`, `DS_VERSION_CORE`, `DS_VERSION_MAJOR/MINOR/PATCH`,
  `DS_HASH`, `DS_DEB_VERSION`, `DS_RELEASE_LINE`; `version_config.h` carries `DS_VERSION` and
  `DS_RELEASE_LINE`; `cot-xlate --version` and `mqtt-xlate --version` print it, and the
  controller, cot-xlate and mqtt-xlate heartbeats report it as `project_version`.

## Builds and the S3 layout

`.github/workflows/sdk-build.yml` (`ci.md` has the step list) is the one build: `workflow_call`
with `flavor`, `build_version`, `release_line`, `ref`, `sdk_uri`, `sdk_sha256`, `sdk_os_release`
and the output `build_prefix`; `workflow_dispatch` with the same minus `flavor`/`ref`. It has no
`push`/`pull_request` trigger and no concurrency group: `pr-checks.yml` and the release
workflows call it and own both. On a lab runner (`[self-hosted, Linux, X64, Ubuntu]`, the
flasher AWS identity) it resolves the SDK (`scripts/sdk-resolve.sh` over `.github/sdk.env`),
ingests it (`scripts/sdk-ingest.sh`), builds every service with `containers/sdk-build.sh`
(`--build-version`/`--release-line` when given), then `scripts-release/artifacts.py
build-manifest --kind install-trees` writes `manifest.json` and `SHA256SUMS` (last) over the
tarball and `sdk-build-info.txt`, the probe runs on the tarball when a version was requested,
and everything is copied to `s3://ds-yocto-artifacts/ds-arm64/<UTC>-<run_id>-standard/` with
`SHA256SUMS` last.

The artifact is one tarball, `ds-sdk-build-<SDK MACHINE>-<sha7>.tar.gz`: `./<recipe>/` for each of
the driver's services (the install tree its recipe's `do_install` produces) plus
`./sdk-build-info.txt` (`ds_commit=`, `ds_version=`, `ds_release_line=`, the SDK, the schemas
commits), nothing else at the top level. The info file is uploaded beside the tarball too.

`manifest.json` (schema 1): `job_id`, `build_datetime`, `buildparams.{flavor, product, machine,
hardened, build_type, build_version, release_line, sdk: {uri, sha256, machine, os_release}}`,
`commit_hashes[]` (first entry `name` is the repo name, `ds`, then `dsensos-sdk` = the
installer's sha256 and `schemas` = the commit built against), `run_url`, `artifacts.debs: []`,
`artifacts.extra[]` (the tarball and the info file: `key`, `sha256`, `bytes`),
`artifacts.install_tree: {key, services}`. `buildparams.sdk` says which toolchain compiled the
build; `os_release` is the OS release it came from (`vX.Y.Z`), `pinned` for the explicit pin, or
the caller's value when a release build reuses its RC's SDK. The bucket is shared with the OS
builds, so S3 keys keep a product segment (`rc/ds/<sha7>/release-manifest.json`,
`release/ds/vX.Y.Z/...`) while git tags do not.

## The SDK: `.github/sdk.env` is bookkeeping

`.github/sdk.env` names the OS product and release line this app line follows (`SDK_OS_PRODUCT`,
`SDK_OS_LINE`: `N.x.x`, `N.M.x` or `latest`) and the SDK MACHINE, or an explicit installer pin
(`SDK_S3_URI` + `SDK_SHA256`, in force until the first OS release ships an SDK). The build
resolves the newest shipped OS release on the line that carries an SDK for the machine at build
time (`scripts/sdk-resolve.sh`, `ci.md`), so the file never changes when the OS ships a release:
it changes only when this app line moves to another OS line. It is the `bookkeeping_files` entry
of `release/config.json`, with the side effect that entails: a commit touching only `versions/`
and `sdk.env` counts as bookkeeping for `release_git.py unmerged` (merge-up keeps the target's
copy, promote does not see it as unmerged work, abandon does not refuse over it). A release build
does not resolve: promote's `check` job reads `builds[].sdk` from the RC's `release-manifest.json`
and passes `sdk_uri`/`sdk_sha256`/`sdk_os_release` per flavor, and the gate refuses a release
whose SDK differs from the RC's. The pilot and `main` follow `vertex` `2.x.x`.

## The jobs

Every job is a workflow file; `gh workflow run <file> --ref <line>`. Control jobs run on the GKE
runner `yocto-spot` (`DS_AWS_EXPECTED_ROLE: gke-embedded-yocto-build`, `scripts-ci/aws-preflight.sh`
first); the ship job on `yocto-ondemand` (never reclaimed mid-copy); the build on the lab
runners. Prologue: `check-tools.sh` (gh, git, jq, python3, aws, plus tar for the install-trees
kind or dpkg-deb for debs), then the App token when `vars.DS_RELEASE_APP_CLIENT_ID` is set, else
`GITHUB_TOKEN` with `TOKEN_KIND=github` (a real run then stops before any push with `lib.sh
no_app_hint` naming the manual command). No `register` jobs: `main` is the default branch, so
every file is dispatchable.

| Workflow | Trigger / inputs | Jobs and what they do |
|---|---|---|
| `release-rc-build.yml` | push to `main`, `[0-9]*.x.x`, `[0-9]*.[0-9]*.x`; dispatch (no inputs, rerun of the tip); concurrency `<workflow>-<sha>` | `plan` (`plan.py`: skip, product, kind, line, rc_version, pending, matrix) → `build` (matrix over the one flavor, `uses: sdk-build.yml` with the RC version and the line; the SDK from `sdk.env`) → `rc-gate` (`rc-gate.sh`, S3 rediscovery by run id) → `publish-rc` (`publish-rc.sh`: draft → assets → pre-release `rc/<sha7>`, S3 index) → `merge-up` (uses `release-merge-up.yml`, minor or patch line, App only) or `merge-up-skipped` |
| `release-promote.yml` | dispatch `bump`, `merge_children`, `dry_run` | `resolve` → `check` (`promote.sh --check`: tip == dispatched sha, green RC on the tip through `walk-versions-only`, children merged via `unmerged`, `promote-plan`, tag absent; concurrency `release-line`; then "The RC's SDK": the RC's `release-manifest.json` asset → `build_matrix` with `sdk_*` per flavor, kept as the `rc-manifest` artifact) → `build` (release version, `uses: sdk-build.yml` with the RC's SDK) → `release-gate` (`rc-gate.sh --kind release --rc-manifest`) → `publish` (`promote.sh --publish`: tag by API, draft → assets → pre-release `vX.Y.Z (staging)` whose notes name each build's SDK, S3 index, one-file bump commit pushed 3 attempts) → `staging-deploy` (stub) |
| `release-ship.yml` | dispatch `version`, `dry_run`; concurrency `release-ship` | `plan` (`ship.sh --plan`, dry run ends here) → `ship` (`environment: production`; copies every object to `release/ds/vX.Y.Z/ds-arm64/standard/<file>`, reads back, `release.json`, flips to the full release) |
| `release-create-branch.yml` | dispatch `version`, `kind`, `seed_from`, `dry_run`; concurrency `release-line` | `create-branch.sh`: line at the tag or at `seed_from` (the tag must be its ancestor), opening commit touching only `versions/ds` |
| `release-merge-up.yml` | workflow_call `child`; dispatch `child`, `pr`, `dry_run` | `resolve` (parent via `lines.py`) → `merge` (`merge-up.sh`: green child tip or `CALLER_SHA`/`CALLER_RUN`, worktree `merge --no-ff`, `release_git.py merge-keep-target` keeps the parent's `versions/` and `.github/sdk.env`, conflict branch `merge-up/<child>/<sha7>` + PR, `--pr` finish after `pr-check`, whose `gh pr view --json statusCheckRollup` read needs the token permissions `checks: read` and `actions: read` together, so the App token step requests both; found 2026-11-10, details in ds-tegra-distro `.ai/release-lines.md`) |
| `release-abandon.yml` | dispatch `line`, `force`, `dry_run` | `resolve` (refuses `main`) → `abandon` (`abandon.sh`: refuses unmerged work or children unless `force`, deletes the ref, `prune-rc.sh --line`: RC releases, tags and S3 objects, keeping any sha a `v*` tag points at) |
| `release-staging-deploy.yml` | workflow_call `request_json` | records the request (the real deploy is a follow-on) |
| `pr-checks.yml` | every PR; dispatch | `build` (uses `sdk-build.yml`, dev version), `release-tooling` (`tests/run.sh`, `check-tools.sh`, `version.py check`, the isolation audit over `release-*.yml`, `scripts-release/` and `sdk-build.yml`), aggregate job named `pr-checks`, always runs, fails unless every job succeeded (a skipped job would satisfy a required check) |

Bookkeeping commits (single-parent, touching only `versions/` and the configured bookkeeping
files) are ignored by `unmerged` and the abandon check; the green-tip walk ignores
`versions/`-only commits (`walk-versions-only`). Merge commits never count as bookkeeping.

## The gate (`rc-gate.sh`, a rubber stamp until ENG-2139)

Per flavor, in S3 by run id: the newest prefix whose `manifest.json` names the flavor;
`buildparams.{product, build_version, flavor}` match the plan; `commit_hashes[name == <repo
name>].commit == sha`; every deb and extra entry has `key`, 64-hex `sha256`, integer `bytes`,
exists with that size, and `SHA256SUMS` agrees (its `manifest.json` line matches the download).
Then by `artifact.kind`:

- `install-trees` (this repo): `artifacts.debs` empty, `artifacts.install_tree {key, services}`
  present with the tarball and the info file listed in `extra`, `services` equal to the config;
  the tarball is downloaded, hashes to its recorded sha256, its top level is exactly the
  configured services plus the info file, the info file says `ds_version=<build_version>` and
  `ds_commit=<sha>`, and the `version_probe` path read with `tar -xzOf` contains the pattern
  (binary-safe grep). The services check is the one a code PR can break: a service added to
  the driver but not to `artifact.services` (or the reverse) fails here, after merge, on every
  RC of the line. ENG-2297 (`ds-eventlog`, PR #597, five red RCs on 1.x.x) added the same
  comparison to `sdk-build.yml` "Check every service is in the driver", so the PR now fails
  first; the checklist is `.ai/sdk-build.md`, "Adding a service". When this error shows up on
  an RC anyway, the fix is the config line, not the gate.
- `debs` (sensor-portal): the package set equals `artifact.debs` exactly; `architecture ==
  deb_arch`; versions follow `deb_version_rule` (`recipe-pv`: `^1\.0\+git`; `deb-version`: equals
  `version.py deb-version <build_version>` with or without a `-r<N>` revision); the `version_probe`
  deb's file contains the pattern.

Both kinds copy `buildparams.sdk` into the build entry as `sdk`. `--kind release --rc-manifest
<the RC's release-manifest.json>` requires each build's `sdk` to equal the RC build's for the
same flavor (an RC that recorded none fails too: rerun its build). It writes
`release-manifest.json` (schema 1: `kind`, `product`, `version`, `pending`, `sha`, `line`,
`run_id`, `run_url`, `builds[].files = {debs, extra, manifest, sha256sums}`, `builds[].sdk`, plus
`rc_run` and `release_run` for `--kind release`), which publish-rc, promote, ship and prune-rc
read; `files.debs` is `[]` here and the tarball sits in `files.extra`, so those four scripts
handle both kinds through the same file groups (their tables say Artifacts, debs plus extra
files). Every miss is one `::error::`; all flavors are checked before exit 1.

## Scripts and tests

`scripts-release/`: `lib.sh` (annotations, `sha7`, `rc_tag`, `product_tag`, `product_label`,
`parse_flavor`, `json_field`, the S3 helpers, `GH_REPO_ARGS`, `gh_release_state`, `no_app_hint`,
`GIT_BOT_NAME`/`GIT_BOT_EMAIL` = `ds-os-release-bot[bot]`, `PRODUCT_PREFIX` read once from the
config), `version.py`, `lines.py`, `plan.py`, `release_git.py`, `artifacts.py` (`build-manifest
--kind debs|install-trees`, `--sdk-*`), `rc-gate.sh`, `publish-rc.sh`, `promote.sh`, `ship.sh`,
`create-branch.sh`, `merge-up.sh`, `abandon.sh`, `prune-rc.sh`, `check-tools.sh`. Signatures live
in each file's header comment. The directory is byte-identical in sensor-portal (the plan is one
shared tooling repo, ENG-2138): nothing in it may name this repo's layout, and a change here is
copied there. The scripts never touch the checkout's working tree: commits happen in worktrees
and temporary clones. `tests/run.sh` runs every `test_*.py` (`test_artifacts.py` among them) and
`test_*.sh` with stub `gh` and `aws` on PATH (`tests/stubs/`, `tests/stubs-tree/`: one bare repo,
trunk `main`), no network, no git identity; the gate, ship and publish-rc tests carry fixtures of
both artifact kinds (tarballs built with `tar`, debs with `dpkg-deb`); `pr-checks` runs it on
every PR. A new test only needs the file.

## Pilot and go-live

The pilot runs live on `versions/ds = 0.0.1` with both rulesets already `active` (the classic
protection on `main` has no App bypass and would refuse the pilot's own bump push, so the
ruleset replaces it before the first promote) and immutable releases off: first RC on `main`, promote `main` with `bump=patch` (`v0.0.1`), `create-branch
version=0.0.1 kind=patch` (`0.0.x`, pending `0.0.2`), a PR into it (RC and automatic merge-up),
a deliberate conflict finished with `pr=<n>`, promote `0.0.x`, ship `v0.0.1` with Raul's
approval, abandon `0.0.x`. Then the go-live PR sets `versions/ds` to `2.0.0`, `prune-rc.sh
--product ds --below 2.0.0` removes the pilot RCs (the pilot releases stay as history), the one
go-live switch flips (`docs/release-admin-setup.md`: immutable releases), and two create-branch runs open the 1.0 lines. `v1.0.0` already exists (hand-made, on the common
ancestor of `main` and `bulbasaur`, the branch carrying the backported 1.0 fixes), so nothing is created for
1.0.0 itself. `create-branch version=1.0.0 kind=patch seed_from=bulbasaur` opens `1.0.x` at that branch's tip with `1.0.1` pending (that branch is
v1.0.0 plus hotfixes, one of which, #581, is not on `main` and reaches `main` by merge-up).
`create-branch version=1.0.0 kind=minor seed_from=main` opens `1.x.x` at `main`'s tip with `1.1.0`
pending, so `1.x.x` and `main` start identical and `main` takes the 2.0 work. `main`'s first
release is `v2.0.0`.
The pilot builds against the explicit `sdk.env` pin; when the first vertex release ships an SDK,
one PR drops the pin lines and the resolver takes over.

## Linear

ENG-2110 (this port), ENG-2126 (the SDK build this sits on), ENG-2138 (one shared tooling repo
instead of three copies, cost/benefit), ENG-2139 (real tests in the gate). The reference
implementation issues are ENG-1930 to ENG-1941 in ds-tegra-distro.
